Pipe A fills at \( \frac{1}{6} \) tank/hour, pipe B at \( \frac{1}{9} \), and drain C empties at \( \frac{1}{12} \).

Net rate:

\[
\frac{1}{6}+\frac{1}{9}-\frac{1}{12}
= \frac{6}{36}+\frac{4}{36}-\frac{3}{36}
= \frac{7}{36}
\]

So the time to fill the tank is:

\[
\frac{1}{\frac{7}{36}}=\frac{36}{7}
\]

ANSWER: \( \frac{36}{7} \)

