If a white key is `flex: 1`, its width is `100% / 14` of the container. `right: -30%` means it extends 30% of a white key's width to the right. `width: 60%` means it covers from `-30%` to `+30%` relative to the right edge of the white key. That's perfectly centered on the boundary between two white keys.

